§ `Section 108 -- Organization meeting of incorporators or directors named in certificate of incorporation`

§§ `s 108(a) The organization meeting`

-- After the filing of the certificate an organization meeting shall be held of the incorporators, or of the board
-- if the initial directors were named in the certificate.
-- src:134 | (a) After the filing of the certificate of incorporation an organization meeting of the incorporator or incorporators, or of the board of directors if the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation, shall be held, either within or without this State, at the call of a majority of the incorporators or directors, as …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(a) (src:134)
GIVEN `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 108(a) the organization meeting is a meeting of the board of directors and not of the incorporators` `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation` MEANS
    `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation`

-- It is held at the call of a majority of the incorporators or directors, as the case may be.
-- src:134 | of incorporation, shall be held, either within or without this State, at the call of a majority of the incorporators or directors, as the case may be, for …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(a) (src:134)
GIVEN `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the incorporators or directors who call the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the incorporators or directors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(a) the call of the organization meeting is made by a majority of the incorporators or directors` `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation` `the number of the incorporators or directors who call the meeting` `the number of the incorporators or directors` MEANS
    -- the base is the incorporators, or, if the initial directors were named, the whole board
    IF `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation`
    THEN `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) `the number of the incorporators or directors who call the meeting` `the number of the incorporators or directors`
    ELSE `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the incorporators`) `the number of the incorporators or directors who call the meeting` `the number of the incorporators or directors`

-- src:134 | the incorporator or incorporators, or of the board of directors if the initial directors were named in the certificate of …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(a) (src:134)
DECLARE `s 108(a) Place of the organization meeting` IS ONE OF
    `within this State`
    `without this State`

-- src:134 | the incorporator or incorporators, or of the board of directors if the initial directors were named in the certificate of …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(a) (src:134)
GIVEN place IS A `s 108(a) Place of the organization meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 108(a) the organization meeting may be held at the place` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `within this State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `without this State` THEN TRUE

-- The purposes: adopting bylaws; electing directors (if the meeting is of the incorporators) to serve or hold
-- office until the first annual meeting or until their successors are elected and qualify; electing officers (if
-- the meeting is of the directors); doing other or further acts to perfect the organization; and transacting such
-- other business as may come before the meeting.
-- src:134 | the case may be, for the purposes of adopting bylaws, electing directors (if the meeting is of the incorporators) to serve or hold office until the first annual meeting of stockholders or until their successors are elected and qualify, electing officers if the meeting is of the directors, doing any other or further acts to perfect the organization of the corporation, and transacting …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(a) (src:134)
DECLARE `s 108(a) Purpose of the organization meeting` IS ONE OF
    `adopting bylaws`
    `electing directors`
    `electing officers`
    `doing any other or further acts to perfect the organization of the corporation`
    `transacting such other business as may come before the meeting`

-- src:134 | the case may be, for the purposes of adopting bylaws, electing directors (if the meeting is of the incorporators) to serve or hold office until the first annual meeting of stockholders or until their successors are elected and qualify, electing officers if the meeting is of the directors, doing any other or further acts to perfect the organization of the corporation, and transacting …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(a) (src:134)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 108(a) Purpose of the organization meeting`
      `the meeting is of the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 108(a) the purpose may be pursued at the organization meeting` purpose `the meeting is of the board of directors` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `adopting bylaws` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `electing directors` THEN NOT (`the meeting is of the board of directors`)
    WHEN `electing officers` THEN `the meeting is of the board of directors`
    WHEN `doing any other or further acts to perfect the organization of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `transacting such other business as may come before the meeting` THEN TRUE

§§ `s 108(b) Notice`

-- The persons calling the meeting shall give each other incorporator or director at least 2 days' notice in writing
-- or by electronic transmission by any usual means of communication, stating the time, place and purposes of the
-- meeting as fixed by the persons calling it.
-- src:135 | (b) The persons calling the meeting shall give to each other incorporator or director, as the case may be, at least 2 days’ notice thereof in writing or by electronic transmission by any usual means of communication, which notice shall state the time, place and purposes of the meeting as …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(b) (src:135)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the notice is in writing or by electronic transmission by a usual means of communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the time, place and purposes of the meeting as fixed by the persons calling it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 108(b) the notice of the organization meeting is sufficient` `the date on which the notice was given` `the date of the meeting` `the notice is in writing or by electronic transmission by a usual means of communication` `the notice states the time, place and purposes of the meeting as fixed by the persons calling it` MEANS
        `the notice is in writing or by electronic transmission by a usual means of communication`
    AND `the notice states the time, place and purposes of the meeting as fixed by the persons calling it`
    AND (`the date of the meeting` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in days` 2) `after` `the date on which the notice was given`))

-- Notice need not be given to anyone who attends the meeting or who waives notice before or after the meeting.
-- src:135 | fixed by the persons calling it. Notice of the meeting need not be given to anyone who attends the meeting or who waives notice either before or …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(b) (src:135)
GIVEN `the person attends the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person waives notice before the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person waives notice after the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 108(b) notice of the meeting need not be given to the person` `the person attends the meeting` `the person waives notice before the meeting` `the person waives notice after the meeting` MEANS
        `the person attends the meeting`
     OR `the person waives notice before the meeting`
     OR `the person waives notice after the meeting`

§§ `s 108(c) Action without a meeting`

-- Unless otherwise restricted by the certificate, any action permitted to be taken at the organization meeting may be
-- taken without a meeting if each incorporator or director, where there is more than 1, or the sole incorporator or
-- director where there is only 1, consents in writing or by electronic transmission. A number of persons that cannot
-- be (fewer than one, more consenting than there are, or a fraction) is not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:136 | (c) Unless otherwise restricted by the certificate of incorporation, (1) any action permitted to be taken at the organization meeting of the incorporators or directors, as the case may be, may be taken without a meeting if each incorporator or director, where there is more than 1, or the sole incorporator or director where there is only 1, consents thereto in writing or …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(c) (src:136)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation restricts action without a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the incorporators or directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of them who consent in writing or by electronic transmission` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(c) the action may be taken without a meeting` `the certificate of incorporation restricts action without a meeting` `the number of the incorporators or directors` `the number of them who consent in writing or by electronic transmission` MEANS
    IF    (`the number of the incorporators or directors` LESS THAN 1)
       OR (NOT (FLOOR `the number of the incorporators or directors` EQUALS `the number of the incorporators or directors`))
       OR (`the number of them who consent in writing or by electronic transmission` LESS THAN 0)
       OR (`the number of them who consent in writing or by electronic transmission` GREATER THAN `the number of the incorporators or directors`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    (NOT (`the certificate of incorporation restricts action without a meeting`))
               AND (`the number of them who consent in writing or by electronic transmission` EQUALS `the number of the incorporators or directors`))

-- A consent may be documented, signed and delivered in any manner permitted by section 116, which is in
-- dg1-s116-documents.l4; this module takes the outcome as the fact that the consent was in writing or by electronic
-- transmission.
-- Any person (whether or not then an incorporator or director) may provide, whether through instruction to an agent
-- or otherwise, that a consent be effective at a future time (including a time determined upon the happening of an
-- event), no later than 60 days after the instruction is given or the provision is made. The consent is deemed given
-- at that time so long as the person is then an incorporator or director and did not revoke the consent before it
-- became effective. A time before the instruction is not a future time (NOTHING).
-- src:136 | Any person (whether or not then an incorporator or director) may provide, whether through instruction to an agent or otherwise, that a consent to action will be effective at a future time (including a time determined upon the happening of an event), no later than 60 days after such instruction is given or such provision is made and such consent shall be deemed to have been given for purposes of this subsection at such effective time so long as such person is then an incorporator or director, as the case may be, and did not revoke the consent prior to such …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(c) (src:136)
GIVEN `the date on which the instruction was given or the provision was made` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the consent is to become effective` IS A DATE
      `the person is then an incorporator or director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person revoked the consent before it became effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(c) the consent given for a future time is deemed given at that time` `the date on which the instruction was given or the provision was made` `the date on which the consent is to become effective` `the person is then an incorporator or director` `the person revoked the consent before it became effective` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the consent is to become effective` LESS THAN `the date on which the instruction was given or the provision was made`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    (`the date on which the consent is to become effective` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` `the date on which the instruction was given or the provision was made`))
               AND `the person is then an incorporator or director`
               AND (NOT (`the person revoked the consent before it became effective`)))

-- Any such consent is revocable prior to its becoming effective: on an earlier date it is, on or after the date it
-- is not, and on the same date it depends on the time of day (NOTHING).
-- src:136 | Any such consent shall be revocable prior to its becoming effective.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(c) (src:136)
GIVEN `the date on which the consent is revoked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the consent is to become effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(c) the consent may still be revoked` `the date on which the consent is revoked` `the date on which the consent is to become effective` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the consent is revoked` LESS THAN `the date on which the consent is to become effective`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the date on which the consent is revoked` GREATER THAN `the date on which the consent is to become effective`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 108(d) An incorporator who is not available`

-- src:137 | (d) If any incorporator is not available to act, then any person for whom or on whose behalf the incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent, may take any action that such incorporator would have been authorized to take under this section or § 107 of this title; provided that any instrument signed by such other person, or any record of the proceedings of a meeting in which such person participated, shall state that such incorporator is not available and the reason therefor, that such incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent for or on behalf of such person, and that such person’s signature on such instrument or participation in such meeting is otherwise authorized and not wrongful.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 108(d) (src:137)
GIVEN `an incorporator is not available to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person for whom or on whose behalf the incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument signed by the person, or the record of the proceedings of the meeting in which the person participated, states that the incorporator is not available and the reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent for or on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the person's signature on the instrument or participation in the meeting is otherwise authorized and not wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 108(d) the person may take the action that the incorporator would have been authorized to take under this section or § 107` `an incorporator is not available to act` `the person is a person for whom or on whose behalf the incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent` `the instrument signed by the person, or the record of the proceedings of the meeting in which the person participated, states that the incorporator is not available and the reason` `it states that the incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent for or on behalf of the person` `it states that the person's signature on the instrument or participation in the meeting is otherwise authorized and not wrongful` MEANS
        `an incorporator is not available to act`
    AND `the person is a person for whom or on whose behalf the incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent`
    AND `the instrument signed by the person, or the record of the proceedings of the meeting in which the person participated, states that the incorporator is not available and the reason`
    AND `it states that the incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent for or on behalf of the person`
    AND `it states that the person's signature on the instrument or participation in the meeting is otherwise authorized and not wrongful`
